{{wikipedia|Eurasian badger}}

===Etymology===
Probably from {{etyl|gem|fi}} {{recons|marþraz|lang=gem-pro}}, cf. Swedish {{term|mård||marten|lang=sv}}. Cognate with Karelian {{term|mäkrä|lang=krl}} and Estonian {{term|mäger|lang=et}}.

